From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 20:35:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] AML: never leave RES_DESKTOP unset, it bricks the GUI

RefreshResolutions only assigns RES_DESKTOP when the current display mode
matches a probed one exactly, refresh rate included, to within FLT_EPSILON.
A current rate the probe list cannot contain therefore leaves RES_DESKTOP
default constructed - 1280x720 at 0.00Hz - and every CreateNewWindow then
fails with "Unable to create window". Kodi restart loops and there is no way
back from the GUI, because there is no GUI.

This is reachable. Leaving the panel at 1080p50hz is enough: the mode survives
a reboot but FRAC_RATE_POLICY resets to 1, the native rate is then reported as
49.95Hz, and no such mode is ever probed because Amlogic only generates
fractional variants for 23.976, 29.97 and 59.94. Recovering it needs modetest
over ssh to put the connector property back.

Fall back to the nearest probed mode of the same size, and say so in the log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
index 3cdb091..e704d3f 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
@@ -438,6 +438,33 @@ void CWinSystemAmlogic::RefreshResolutions()
       CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(RES_DESKTOP) = res;
     }
   }
+
+  // The match above is exact, so a current rate the probe list cannot contain
+  // leaves RES_DESKTOP default constructed at 1280x720@0.00 and every
+  // CreateNewWindow then fails - Kodi cannot start at all, with no way back
+  // from the GUI. 1080p50hz with FRAC_RATE_POLICY still 1 reports 49.95Hz and
+  // does exactly that, because fractional variants are only generated for
+  // 23.976/29.97/59.94. Fall back to the nearest mode of the same size.
+  RESOLUTION_INFO& desktop = CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(RES_DESKTOP);
+  if (desktop.fRefreshRate <= 0.0f && !resolutions.empty())
+  {
+    const RESOLUTION_INFO* best = nullptr;
+    for (const auto& res : resolutions)
+    {
+      if (res.iScreenWidth != resDesktop.iScreenWidth ||
+          res.iScreenHeight != resDesktop.iScreenHeight)
+        continue;
+      if (best == nullptr || fabs(res.fRefreshRate - resDesktop.fRefreshRate) <
+                                 fabs(best->fRefreshRate - resDesktop.fRefreshRate))
+        best = &res;
+    }
+    if (best == nullptr)
+      best = &resolutions.front();
+
+    CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "{}: no mode matches the current display rate {:f} Hz, using {}",
+              __FUNCTION__, resDesktop.fRefreshRate, best->strMode);
+    desktop = *best;
+  }
 }
 
 void CWinSystemAmlogic::UpdateResolutions()
